@startuml
title Xen FDT review-fix API flow

participant "Xen" as Xen
participant "arm64 reset.S" as Reset
participant ".noinit handoff\nz_arm64_xen_fdt_addr\nz_arm64_xen_fdt_size" as NoInit
participant "z_prep_c()" as Prep
participant "xen_copy_fdt()" as Copy
participant "private saved copy\nstatic xen_fdt[]\nxen_fdt_size" as Saved
participant "runtime consumer\nFDT probe / Xen code" as Consumer

Xen -> Reset: enter boot CPU\nx0 = Xen-generated FDT address
Reset -> NoInit: store raw FDT address
Reset -> NoInit: read totalsize at x0 + 4\nstore raw big-endian size
note right of NoInit
The handoff slots are internal early-boot state.
They survive arch_data_copy(), but consumers should not use them directly.
end note

Reset -> Prep: branch to C preparation
Prep -> Prep: arch_bss_zero()
Prep -> Prep: arch_data_copy()
Prep -> Copy: xen_copy_fdt()

Copy -> NoInit: read preserved address and size
Copy -> Copy: check FDT magic
alt invalid magic
	Copy -> Copy: LOG_ERR + k_panic()
else size exceeds CONFIG_XEN_FDT_MAX_SIZE
	Copy -> Copy: LOG_ERR + k_panic()
else valid FDT
	Copy -> Saved: arch_early_memcpy(valid bytes)
	Copy -> Saved: record copied size
end

Consumer -> Saved: get_xen_fdt_ptr(&size)
Saved --> Consumer: stable Zephyr-owned FDT copy\nand copied byte count
note right of Consumer
The runtime probe validated this path by checking magic,
totalsize, selected nodes, and FDT_END, then printing FDT PROBE PASS.
end note

@enduml
